 {"id":"adi-mt002-nyquist","type":"manufacturer_tutorial","title":"MT-002 — What the Nyquist Criterion Means to Your Sampled Data System Design","organization":"Analog Devices","url":"https://www.analog.com/media/en/training-seminars/tutorials/mt-002.pdf","verification_status":"verified_directly","locator":"Sections on aliasing, Nyquist zones and anti-alias filter transition/attenuation trade-offs","curricular_function":"Support the analog anti-alias requirement and joint selection of sampling frequency and transition band.","coverage":[4,5],"limitations":"Sampling tutorial; U4 uses it only to specify the analog interface, while quantization/ADC details are deferred to U5."},
